hile you're hearing it  and while you're reading it you're  watching what we think might have been  going on in emily's life or in her mind  when she was writing that poem uh and it  just brings each and every line of those  poems to life and uh  yeah i mean they're incredible so to be  able to to voice them has  been very exciting  what's it like to have had the  collaboration the partnership with elena  smith for three seasons how does the  actor show runner relationship compared  to  the actor director relationship you've  had on films  elena and i had a conversation uh it was  actually really the first time that we  sat down in person uh before we started  shooting and we were in new york city  and  i was a little  um  let's just say i had never experienced  any kind of director switching uh  while playing one character um and i was  i didn't know how to feel about it i was  obviously very excited about everybody  that we were about to bring onto the  show but i was a little nervous in  developing this character having so many  people to do that with before i had the  chance to feel like i had it myself um  was a little daunting and elena had  looked at me and said listen  you and i  are here i am not going anywhere these  directors might be switching out every  two two and a half weeks whatever it was  but i  will be here and from that point on our  collaboration has really been  um  non-stop in a way and and it's been  really amazing to sort of get into her  head and and be a part of this vision  that she has had in there for so long um  and she just is she's i call her my  emily dickinson encyclopedia she just  like anytime i have any questions she's  got the answer um but she's been really  awesome uh through this whole process  and i'm i'm again just so honored that i  was able to be a part of her vision  after finishing up with dickinson you  got to jump into doing hawkeye  what was it actually like to make a  marvel series compared to what you  thought it might be or what you expected  going into it  uh well first of all it was definitely  um  wild going from uh  an 1860s period drama comedy wearing  corsets and  all that  going straight into  the marvel universe wearing a  superhero suit and  i was in the middle of these car chases  and these crazy action-packed um  stunt driven scenes uh that was took me  a second to uh wrap my head around that  but  so amazing i feel so again lucky to be a  part of something so  special and kate bishop is a character  that i  continue to discover more and more about  that i just love i mean i think i can't  love her anymore and then i  discover something new and it's  mainly exciting to see that this is a  character the fans have wanted to see  come to life for a very long time and um  yeah it's it's a good one i'm ready for  everyone to see it  how much has kevin feige and marvel told  you about the arc of the character going  forward do you feel like you have a  sense of what could come next for her or  do you feel as in the dark as the fans  uh i  well the thing about i think they're  they're you might be able to get a sense  by the end of uh of hawkeye um what her  deal is and it's been really exciting to  sort of develop her and and  um introduce her story and her  background to the world uh through this  show uh and i'm just very excited for  people to see it and i can't wait to  hear what they think  i love the relationship between emily  and lavinia it's  especially in this season they're  they're really both just having to be  there for each other  what was the experience of forming that  sister bond as characters and and as  actors because it's just there's  something so lovely about watching the  two of you thank you so much anna and i  have had such a fun time together i i  through seasons one and two  and of course three uh i anytime i got  to have a scene with anna i was always  especially  excited i think she  is so incredible in this show and she  balances this very fine line of  this this this dramatic and comedic  performance um that i mean every time i  i will read through an episode i  am just like instantly excited about  what lavinia gets to do right and then  when i get to actually see anna do it  and play through these moments that are  actually very complicated and and  layered um  is is it's always she really blows me  away and and um  i  love that in this season we really get  to see  emily open up to lavinia in a way that  she hasn't before  and we get to see lavinia  accept not that she ever  didn't in the past but we get to see her  really appreciate the fact that her  sister is who she is and and for the  first time there's this connection where  we see them see each other we see  lavinia see emily and although in the  past you know she's kind of rolled her  eyes and thought my sister is so  eccentric and she just does her own  thing and she's so you know we are so  not on the same page i think she finally  realizes that she is who she is and she  loves her for who she is and it's a  really beautiful moment  emily and sue were in a bit of a love  bubble in season two because nobody  really knew about them but in season  three  it seems that sue is making some more  demands on emily what did you enjoy  about  that dynamic this season and really sort  of getting to see where that whole  journey ends up  well i always i've always loved that  whenever emily and sue are together they  really are  their truest selves  and  in season three  they're definitely in um very specific  points in their own personal lives but  sue continues to be this person for  emily that pushes her to be true to  herself and and  um own her take ownership of herself and  so she kind of pushes her in this season  a little bit and like you said she makes  these demands that that she hasn't in  the past and emily respects her and  emily has this this  love for her that is so  deeply rooted um and regardless of where  she is in her life and and how she's  interconnected into the family she has  this love for her that can never be  diminished and um  it'll never go away and it's a really  really  lovely and  beautiful relationship and i am so um  pleased with how we've played through it  how do you feel about the final moment  and what the last parting  moment is that we get to see of emily  it's very bittersweet and i'll never  forget shooting it um  and sort of being  on my own uh and having this real moment  of  looking out into  the future and  not necessarily knowing what it holds  and and again  this show has continued to um  sort  of shock me or or maybe even scare me a  little bit with these parallels that  they've that they have in in our world  now um and in my life personally and the  last day of shooting anything is is like  i mean  you're like you mean i don't have to  show up here tomorrow morning and and be  on time for something and and give  myself to something else and be prepared  like what am i going to do with my life  i this is it  and i have this moment of like pure  hope and and and excitement towards the  future and with the civil war being the  time that emily wrote the majority of  her poems having that moment where we  get to see her look out into this world  of what is to come  uh is really beautiful and um  yeah it was a real moment for me as well  because i i feel i had a similar one  well thank you beautiful work in this i  appreciate it thanks so much  thank you  you
 

